<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="249" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>One customer-stamp template (owner D19) — delete `stacks/model2-full.bicep` + its parameter files, `deploy-infrastructure.yml` validates `customer.bicep`, and fix the five `customer.bicep` defects the comparison found</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T249 (owner decision D19, open item O5)</phase>
    <gate>startable after T225b (file overlap: customer.json, controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep); must land before T242</gate>
    <status>in-progress</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Deletes Bicep stacks + parameter files, edits a CI workflow, edits customer.bicep (deployed by H2a) and ArmDeploymentRunner (.cs) + its tests.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fully specified by the O5 comparison (file and line evidence below); the risk is completeness across Bicep, workflow, runner and docs, not judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches .claude/ (azure-deploy skill, provisioning patterns, CHANGELOG) — main-session-only; file overlap with T225b and T248</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, bicep, infrastructure, ci-workflows, l2-controlplane, testing, model1-dedicated</tags>
    <deps>225b</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Make `infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep` the only customer-stamp template: delete `stacks/model2-full.bicep` and the
    parameter files that only feed it, reduce `deploy-infrastructure.yml` to validating `customer.bicep`, and fix the
    `customer.bicep` defects the 2026-10-02 comparison found, so T242 can change the Redis module without breaking CI.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer (Bicep, GitHub Actions, .NET 10 L2 control plane). Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    No file in the repo deploys or parameterizes `model2-full`; the infrastructure workflow lints and compiles
    `customer.bicep` on PR/push and has no what-if or deploy stage; `customer.bicep` wires SignalR and the control-plane
    role grant to real principals, logs Key Vault diagnostics, has no dead `platformKeyVaultName` input and produces no
    per-deploy tag drift; docs that called `model2-full` current point at `customer.bicep`.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Owner D19 (2026-10-02): `customer.bicep` (H2a) is the only customer-stamp template. The O5 comparison found that
      `stacks/model2-full.bicep` deploys no live environment (`stacks/dev.bicepparam:14-19`: the dev env is hand-built and
      not managed by it) and cannot deploy as written: customerIds over 8 chars in all three bicepparams (`m2f:35`), the
      Azure-reserved `-sb` Service Bus suffix (`m2f:159`), no Cosmos (the BFF refuses to start without
      `CosmosPersistence__Endpoint`), KV references to secrets nothing writes, no `AZURE_CLIENT_ID` pin, one shared
      subscription (`deploy-infrastructure.yml:54-57`) contradicting amended ADR-027. `deploy-infrastructure.yml` compiles
      every `stacks/*.bicep` on each PR, and `model2-full` passes `sku`/`capacity`/`subnetId`/`enableRdbPersistence` to
      `modules/redis.bicep` (`m2f:139-147`) — so T242's Redis module replacement would break CI while it exists.
      customer.bicep defects found by the same comparison: (1) SignalR receives `bffPrincipalId` (`customer.bicep:537`),
      which H2a never passes, and `signalr.bicep:83` disables key auth → no BFF access when enabled; (2)
      `controlPlaneUamiPrincipalId` is never passed (no match in src/), so the Website Contributor grant on the BFF app is
      never created and PRQ-E-05's "emitted on every stamp" is false; (3) Key Vault diagnostic logging is not wired
      (`:252-265`); (4) `platformKeyVaultName` is only echoed as an output (`:885`); (5) the default tags include
      `utcNow()`, so every upgrade what-if shows a tag Modify.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/stacks/model2-full.bicep, stacks/model2-full.json (delete)</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/stacks/dev.bicepparam, staging.bicepparam, prod.bicepparam (delete)</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/parameters/model2-customer-template.bicepparam (delete)</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/customer-deployment.bicepparam (delete — verify its `using` target first)</file>
      <file>.github/workflows/deploy-infrastructure.yml</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep (+ customer.json)</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/modules/signalr.bicep, modules/key-vault.bicep, modules/monitoring.bicep (read; edit only if wiring requires)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/BicepInfraDeploy/ArmDeploymentRunner.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Handlers/ArmDeploymentRunnerTests.cs</file>
      <file>scripts/tests/bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1</file>
      <file>scripts/provisioning-prereqs/prereqs.yaml (PRQ-E-05)</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/INFRASTRUCTURE-PACKAGING-STRATEGY.md, docs/architecture/AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md, docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md, docs/guides/AI-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md, docs/guides/AI-MONITORING-DASHBOARD.md, infrastructure/README.md, provisioning-runs/_templates/handler-log.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/azure-deploy/SKILL.md, .claude/patterns/provisioning/INDEX.md, .claude/CHANGELOG.md (main session)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/model1-dedicated-remediation-plan.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-027-subscription-isolation-and-dataverse-solution-management.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-020-versioning.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Upgrade what-if drift" location="T225a POML notes (bff-runtime-rbac CR-1); ArmWhatIfDriftDetector">
        Any value that changes on every deploy (timestamps) or a rewritten deployed description shows as a Modify on an
        existing stamp's upgrade what-if, which the drift detector rejects.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner D19 (2026-10-02)">
      Delete, do not repoint: `stacks/model2-full.{bicep,json}`, `stacks/{dev,staging,prod}.bicepparam`,
      `parameters/model2-customer-template.bicepparam`, `customer-deployment.bicepparam` (confirm each file's `using`
      target is `model2-full` first; a file that uses something else is reported, not deleted). Git history keeps them.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D19 + project CLAUDE.md (r1 owns its workflow changes since ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1 closed)">
      `deploy-infrastructure.yml`: keep a validate job that lints all Bicep and compiles `customer.bicep`
      (`az bicep build --outfile`); remove the what-if and deploy stages and the dispatch inputs that feed them. Customer
      stamps deploy only through H2a.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ArmWhatIfDriftDetector / T225a CR-1">
      Every `customer.bicep` change must leave an existing stamp's upgrade what-if free of spurious Modify operations:
      do not rewrite deployed role-assignment descriptions; replace `utcNow()` tags with values that are stable for a given
      customer + environment.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 (MI for app-only outbound) + D13">
      SignalR access is granted to the stamp UAMI (`uami.outputs.principalId`); never re-enable key auth. The control-plane
      principal passed to `controlPlaneUamiPrincipalId` comes from the existing L2 principal Worker option (T245b) — do
      not add a new option.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="scope">
      No feature from `model2-full` other than Key Vault diagnostic logging is ported (dashboard/alerts, VNet, autoscale,
      AI Foundry stay out — D19). Redis untouched (T242). OpenAI deployments parameter untouched (T247). Content Safety
      untouched (T246). `controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` untouched (T228). No change to `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api`.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Any file slated for deletion is referenced by a live deployment pipeline, another project's worktree, or a `using` target other than `model2-full` → STOP and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>Removing `platformKeyVaultName` or changing the tags makes `ArmTemplateInspector`, `RunContextContractTests` or the what-if drift tests fail for a reason other than the intended change → STOP; do not loosen the test.</trigger>
    <trigger>The L2 principal option from T245b is not available to `ArmDeploymentRunner` without a new DI dependency on an unrelated module → STOP and report the options.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">0 behind origin/master; `git grep -n "model2-full\|customer-deployment.bicepparam\|model2-customer-template"` → categorized hit list in notes.</step>
    <step order="1">Delete the template + parameter files (after the `using` check).</step>
    <step order="2">`deploy-infrastructure.yml` → validate-only; keep its PR/push triggers on `infrastructure/bicep/**`.</step>
    <step order="3">`customer.bicep`: SignalR principal; `controlPlaneUamiPrincipalId` passed from `ArmDeploymentRunner.BuildParametersPayload`; Key Vault diagnostic setting to the stamp's Log Analytics; remove `platformKeyVaultName` (param + output) and its payload entry if any; stable tags. Recompile `customer.json` (`--outfile`).</step>
    <step order="4">ArmDeploymentRunnerTests: the payload now carries `controlPlaneUamiPrincipalId`; a missing L2 principal fails the same way other required options do. PRQ-E-05 text corrected; `validate.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="5">Docs and `.claude` references repointed to `customer.bicep` (main session for `.claude`), CHANGELOG entry; `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` stack list/comments.</step>
    <step order="6">Verify: every remaining Bicep compiles and checked-in JSON = fresh compile; `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` PASS; ControlPlane builds 0/0; ControlPlane.Tests no failures beyond the 6 T221 baseline; ArchTests pass; actionlint/yaml check on the workflow if available.</step>
    <step order="7">Step 9.5 gates. Close: POML notes, TASK-INDEX `✅ [done]`, plan §7 T249 + §3/§4 rows it settles, current-task.md, drift check. Commit + push.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="az">`az bicep build --outfile` / `az bicep lint`</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + test ControlPlane and ArchTests</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1, prereqs validate.ps1, check-task-status-drift.ps1</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="file-deleted">stacks/model2-full.{bicep,json}; stacks/{dev,staging,prod}.bicepparam; parameters/model2-customer-template.bicepparam; customer-deployment.bicepparam</output>
    <output type="file-modified">deploy-infrastructure.yml; customer.bicep (+ customer.json); ArmDeploymentRunner.cs (+ tests); prereqs.yaml; docs; .claude skill/pattern/CHANGELOG</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`git grep model2-full` returns only historical records (dated notes, CHANGELOG, POMLs); none of the deleted files exist.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`deploy-infrastructure.yml` lints all Bicep and compiles `customer.bicep` on PR/push; it has no what-if job, no deploy job and no dispatch input naming a stack.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`customer.bicep`: SignalR's data-plane role targets the stamp UAMI principal; the Website Contributor grant is created whenever `controlPlaneUamiPrincipalId` is non-empty and `ArmDeploymentRunner` always sends it; Key Vault has a diagnostic setting to the stamp Log Analytics workspace; `platformKeyVaultName` no longer exists; no tag value is computed from the deploy time.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArmDeploymentRunner tests: the payload contains `controlPlaneUamiPrincipalId` = the configured L2 principal; the Model 1 arm still fails closed (T2 unchanged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every remaining Bicep file compiles; each checked-in ARM JSON equals a fresh compile; `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` PASS; prereqs `validate.ps1` OK with PRQ-E-05 describing what customer.bicep actually emits.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane projects build 0/0; ControlPlane.Tests no failures beyond the 6 T221 baseline; ArchTests pass; Redis, OpenAI deployments, Content Safety, `controlplane-subscription-rbac.bicep` and the BFF unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the changed runner payload contract and the negative case named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the POML notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Filed 2026-10-02 from plan §7 T249 / owner D19 (open item O5). Evidence: the O5 comparison (main-session record in
    plan §2 D19). Dev/demo environments are hand-built and stay outside IaC until the D13 follow-on.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load every file in knowledge/files before Step 1. Follow task-execute; FULL rigor; Step 9.5 gates are mandatory.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
